## Issue 1: Unnecessary Vec Allocation in `normalized_code`

**File:** `crates/ragent-bench/src/suites/metrics.rs`  
**Lines:** 54-61

**Current Code:**
```rust
pub(crate) fn normalized_code(value: &str) -> String {
    value
        .split_whitespace()
        .collect::<Vec<_>>()  // Unnecessary allocation
        .join(" ")
        .trim()
        .to_string()
}
```

**Problem:** The function collects split whitespace into a `Vec` just to join it. This allocates memory for the Vec and all string slices, then immediately discards it.

**Suggested Fix:**
```rust
pub(crate) fn normalized_code(value: &str) -> String {
    value
        .split_whitespace()
        .fold(String::new(), |mut acc, s| {
            if !acc.is_empty() {
                acc.push(' ');
            }
            acc.push_str(s);
            acc
        })
        .trim()
        .to_string()
}
```

Or using `intersperse` from itertools if available in the crate.

