## Issue 5: Linear Search in `is_language_label`

**File:** `crates/ragent-bench/src/suites/mod.rs`  
**Lines:** 149-175

**Current Code:**
```rust
fn is_language_label(line: &str) -> bool {
    matches!(
        line.trim().to_ascii_lowercase().as_str(),
        "c++" | "cpp" | "c#" | // ... 20+ more patterns
    )
}
```

**Problem:** This creates a new String via `to_ascii_lowercase()` then does a linear match through 20+ patterns. While not performance-critical (called once per code block), it could be more efficient.

**Suggested Fix:** Use a static HashSet or match on bytes without allocation:
```rust
use std::sync::OnceLock;

fn is_language_label(line: &str) -> bool {
    static LANG_SET: OnceLock<std::collections::HashSet<&'static str>> = OnceLock::new();
    let set = LANG_SET.get_or_init(|| {
        ["c++", "cpp", "c#", /* ... */].into_iter().collect()
    });
    set.contains(line.trim().to_ascii_lowercase().as_str())
}
```

Or simply lowercase once:
```rust
fn is_language_label(line: &str) -> bool {
    let lower = line.trim().to_ascii_lowercase();
    matches!(lower.as_str(), /* ... */)
}
```

